# Cloudflare Pages / Workers Static Assets redirects
#
# Rewrites /r/<code> straight to the CANONICAL, extensionless path
# "/referral/page" (not "/referral/page.html"), passing the code as a
# query parameter (?code=...).
#
# Why not target "/referral/page.html"? Because Wrangler's
# "html_handling": "auto-trailing-slash" setting issues a REAL, second
# redirect from "/referral/page.html" to "/referral/page" (stripping the
# .html). That second redirect was found to DROP THE QUERY STRING
# entirely (not just the path), so "?code=..." got lost along the way
# and the page ended up with no code at all. By targeting the
# extensionless canonical path directly, the rewrite already matches
# what html_handling expects, so that second redirect never fires and
# the query string survives.
#
# NOTE: target filename intentionally is NOT "index.html" -- Wrangler's
# _redirects validator has a known false-positive bug (workers-sdk#11824)
# that flags ANY rewrite target ending in "index.html" as an infinite loop,
# even when it isn't one. Renaming the file sidesteps that check.
/r/:code    /referral/page?code=:code   200
